From: Fleurs Nix configuration
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve request-scoped queued GNOME unlocks on oo7 0.7.1

Upstream already has optional secrets and atomic prompt/session IDs. Keep
independent actions, target lists and cancellation for overlapping requests;
do not share one prompt. Recheck the collection when GCR selects each queued
request, propagating action failures instead of reporting false completion.
The native unencrypted-keyring path validates plaintext, so the obsolete
blanket prohibition on unlocking without a secret is no longer needed.

